Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Frank-Lloyd-Wright.md` and appended the `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits.

**The two biggest issues:**

1. **No Type 5 rebuttal.** The draft defeats a Type 4 reading twice and never names Five once. That's the packet's #1 content requirement, and it matters more than the packet says: every free aggregator on page one of the type query asserts 5w4, so the reader we're arguing to arrives holding the opposing answer. One paragraph beside the existing Type 4 rebuttal fixes it.

2. **The Mamah section has no felt interior.** It's written as a prosecutor's ledger ("Read it again. Four months... New lover installed. Construction crew paid.") and then explained with type theory — the reader learns what Wright did and nothing about what it cost him. The record has the missing beat: he filled her casket with flowers cut from her own garden, filled in the grave himself, and refused a marker, writing *"Why mark the spot where desolation ended and began?"* That's the empathy turn the draft lacks, and it's better evidence for the Seven thesis than the four-month timeline. It also exposes a factual wobble: the conclusion says he buried her "on his own land, where he could keep her in the frame," but she's in the Lloyd Jones family cemetery at Unity Chapel and he refused the marker outright.

**Two things worth flagging beyond the notes:**

- The draft is ~5,020 words against the 4,500 ceiling, with 5 lint fails (word count, 47 prose em-dashes, 5 contrast-pair engines, missing Rabbit Hole, meta_title lacks a searchable head term). Nothing can be added until something is cut.
- **The draft's own ledgers are unreliable.** The FORMULA FINGERPRINT LEDGER self-reports 3 contrast pairs where lint counts 5, and the DISTRIBUTION LEDGER reports "No Rabbit Hole present" as though that passes. The next pass shouldn't trust them.

The largest expansion opportunity I found that isn't in the packet: the piece opens on Hib Johnson and gives him a full H2, but never mentions that Johnson was already building the S.C. Johnson Administration Building when that roof leaked on him, and commissioned the Research Tower from Wright afterward. The client took the insult and kept paying — which answers the strongest critic with evidence instead of the draft's own assertion that "the cantilever was the achievement."

Sources for the checks: [Mamah Borthwick burial](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mamah_Borthwick), [John Lloyd Wright](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Lloyd_Wright), [Johnson Wax Headquarters](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnson_Wax_Headquarters), [Wingspread](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wingspread)
